      "      --library <library>",
      "          Object library root, such as an SDK's rawdata/objects: its objects found placed in the static geometry and its trees found as tree models are placed by reference and copied beside the objects, and its surfaces' pairings of engine and compiler shaders break ties between compiler shaders that fit; repeatable",
      "      --spawn <spawn>",
      "          Root spawn whose objects on the level replace level.spawn's entities, read from spawns/<spawn>.spawn beside the level's levels directory; all.spawn by default where it exists",
      "  -f, --force",
      "          Overwrite an existing .level, its parts, its sidecar, its objects and textures, and remove the parts and objects of the level's own an earlier decompile wrote that this one does not; without it, the scene or the level's objects already there are refused before the level is read",
      "  -j, --jobs <JOBS>",
      "          How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' [default: auto]",
      "  -h, --help",
